            <ArticleTitle>A 47-year-old stem cell transplant recipient with fever, cough and chest pain.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>144-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Infections and malignancies are among the most serious complications that follow organ or stem cell transplantation. They may have a mild course, and nonspecific and overlapping manifestations. The present article describes a case of symptomatic nodular pulmonary disease that complicated hematopoietic stem cell transplantation. It was diagnosed to be post-transplant lymphoproliferative disorder, a potential sequela of immunosuppression and a very difficult entity to treat in profoundly immunosuppressed patients.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
